(area "preferences" :when "the app must look or behave differently for this user: sidebar, status bar, chat display, what shows under a message (tokens, time, model), input helpers, motion, font or desktop app")

(memory "internal/preferences/layout" :when "sidebar entries must be reordered, moved between sidebars or hidden, or status bar items moved, hidden or left as gaps"
  (format nil "- Two sidebars, left and right. :sidebar is left one's entries, top first;
  :sidebar-right is right one's. Each entry sits in one. Names come from
(preferences) .
(preferences/set :sidebar '(\"README.md\" \"chat\")) moves those two to top of
  left, pulling them from right if there; rest keep their order.
(preferences/set :sidebar-right '(\"tests\")) moves tests to top of right.
  Same entry in both lists errors. User also drags entries within a sidebar,
  across to other one, or in preferences page.
- :hidden is every sidebar entry hidden. Replaces whole list:
(preferences/set :hidden '(\"tests\" \"ui\")) hides those two, shows rest.
'() shows all. User also toggles them in preferences page.
- :status-bar is bottom bar's ~d slots, left to right. Items:
  ~{~s~^ ~}. Each empty slot is gap with own name: ~{~s~^ ~}.
(preferences/set :status-bar '(~s ~s ~s)) puts named slots first,
  in that order, keeps rest in order. User also drags them on bar or in
  preferences.
- :status-bar-hidden is every bottom bar item hidden. Replaces whole list:
(preferences/set :status-bar-hidden '(~s)) hides
  that one. '() shows all."
    *preferences-status-bar-slots* *preferences-status-bar-items* *preferences-status-bar-gaps*
    (car (cdr *preferences-status-bar-items*)) (car *preferences-status-bar-gaps*) (car *preferences-status-bar-items*)
    (car *preferences-status-bar-items*)))

(memory "internal/preferences/metadata" :when "the user wants to show or hide what appears under a message: input, output or cached tokens, time, duration, steps, model or provider"
  (format nil "- :metadata is what shows under each message. Ids: ~{~a ~a~^, ~}.
- Token counts are :metadata ids. :input key of preferences/set is chat input
  helpers, not tokens.
- (preferences/set :metadata '(~a t)) shows that one, leaves
  rest as they were. nil hides. Name several in one plist.
- (preferences) shows what is on now. Unknown id errors, naming valid ones."
    *preferences-metadata* (car *preferences-metadata*)))

(memory "internal/preferences/chat" :when "the chat must change: which helpers the input runs, or where a trace opens"
  (format nil "- :input is helpers chat input runs while user types. Ids: ~{~a ~a~^, ~}.
(preferences/set :input '(~a nil)) turns that one off.
- :trace-beside-chat t opens chat's trace in tab right of chat whenever chat
  opens; nil opens trace only when asked. For developers:
(preferences/set :trace-beside-chat t) .
- :trace-link t shows \"show in trace\" on message metadata; opens trace at
  that message. nil hides it: (preferences/set :trace-link nil) .
- (preferences) shows what is on now."
    *preferences-input* (car *preferences-input*)))

(memory "internal/preferences/motion" :when "animations must change: how the sidebar moves on a drag, or whether panels animate when they open or split"
  "- :motion is how sidebar animates that drag. (motions) gives alist of
(id . description) to choose from. System asks for reduced motion: nothing
  animates, whatever :motion says.
- :panel-motion t animates panels as they open, split, switch tab; nil keeps
  them still: (preferences/set :panel-motion nil) . Reduced motion wins here too.")

(memory "internal/preferences/desktop" :when "the desktop app must close to the tray or start at login, or stop doing so"
  (format nil "- (desktop-preferences) gives desktop app's own as plist of ~{~a~^ ~} .
  Live on user's machine, not in app. Work only while desktop app connected;
  else error says no desktop app connected.
- :close-to-tray t keeps desktop app running in tray when window closes; nil
  quits: (desktop-preferences/set :close-to-tray nil) .
- :open-at-login t starts desktop app hidden in tray at login:
(desktop-preferences/set :open-at-login t) ."
    *preferences-desktop-keys*))

(memory "internal/preferences/set" :when "a preference change just failed, or the agent must read or change the font or a chat input helper"
  (format nil "- (preferences) gives plist of ~{~a~^ ~} .
- Each workspace keeps own set, like theme; change here leaves other workspaces
  alone. Theme: see (settings) .
- (fonts) gives alist of (id . name) to choose from.
- (preferences/set :font ~s) changes only keys you give.
- :metadata and :input take toggle plist; toggles merge, ids not named keep
  their value. Font id must be one (fonts) lists. Metadata and input ids must
  be ones (preferences) already lists. Unknown one errors, naming valid ids.
- Quote toggle plist, or keywords read as call: '(~a t) ."
    *preferences-keys* (car (car (fonts))) (car *preferences-metadata*)))
